From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gael Julien <jgm509@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:06:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: skip vdevs without a link sta in chain RSSI stats

The firmware answers a WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT request with an
entry for every vdev on the pdev, including AP vdevs and stations that
aren't associated. ath12k_wmi_tlv_rssi_chain_parse() returns -EPROTO for
any entry whose vdev has no link sta for its BSSID, which drops the
whole event:

  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0003:01:00.0: not found link sta with bssid xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx for rssi chain
  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0003:01:00.0: failed to pull fw stats: -71
  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0003:01:00.0: time out while waiting for fw stats done

So on a radio that runs a station next to APs (for example a WiFi
uplink), every station statistics query waits for the stats timeout
(1 s, or 3 s for fw_stats_done) while holding the wiphy lock. Any
nl80211 query on the same wiphy waits behind it: on a QCN9274 with
seven interfaces, "iwinfo <ifname> info" takes 3.1 s per interface.

Skip those entries instead, and mark the event as a per-chain RSSI
event before looking at the entries, so the request still completes
when no entry matches.

Tested on Askey SBE1V1K and CBE1V1K (IPQ9574 + QCN9274) with a WiFi
uplink next to the APs: "iwinfo <ifname> info" went from 1.1 s (SBE)
and 3.1 s (CBE) per interface to 0.03 s, the stats errors are gone and
the station signal is still reported.

Signed-off-by: Gael Julien <jgm509@protonmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c | 24 +++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -8487,10 +8487,19 @@ static int ath12k_wmi_tlv_rssi_chain_par
 		return -EPROTO;
 	}
 
+	/* The firmware reports per-chain RSSI for every vdev on the pdev,
+	 * including AP vdevs and stations that aren't connected. Only a
+	 * connected station has a link sta for its BSSID; skip the other
+	 * entries instead of failing the whole event, which would leave the
+	 * request waiting for its timeout.
+	 */
+	stats->stats_id = WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT;
+
 	arvif = ath12k_mac_get_arvif(ar, vdev_id);
 	if (!arvif) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab, "not found vif for vdev id %d\n", vdev_id);
-		return -EPROTO;
+		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
+			   "rssi chain: no vif for vdev id %d, skipping\n", vdev_id);
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
@@ -8500,10 +8509,10 @@ static int ath12k_wmi_tlv_rssi_chain_par
 	guard(spinlock_bh)(&ab->base_lock);
 	arsta = ath12k_link_sta_find_by_addr(ab, arvif->bssid);
 	if (!arsta) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab,
-			    "not found link sta with bssid %pM for rssi chain\n",
-			    arvif->bssid);
-		return -EPROTO;
+		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
+			   "rssi chain: no link sta with bssid %pM, skipping\n",
+			   arvif->bssid);
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(arsta->chain_signal) >
@@ -8512,8 +8521,6 @@ static int ath12k_wmi_tlv_rssi_chain_par
 	for (j = 0; j < ARRAY_SIZE(arsta->chain_signal); j++)
 		arsta->chain_signal[j] = le32_to_cpu(stats_rssi->rssi_avg_beacon[j]);
 
-	stats->stats_id = WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT;
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
